# Thrill of Possibility: "As an additional cost to cast this spell, discard a card" (CR 601.2b, 118.8). The discard is a cost
# (CR 118.3) that can't be paid with the spell itself, which has left the hand (CR 601.2a) - and exactly one card is discarded
# (ruling 2023-02-04). On turn 1 Bot1 empties its hand onto the battlefield, so the Thrill is refused though its mana is there
# to pay; on turn 2 it draws an Island, discards it as the cost, and draws two cards (CR 608.2c).

